  "raw_text": "207\n\nMihta sakbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto shake hands\n \n/ dar la mano\n, estrechar la mano\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nMihta\n \nsihbaia\n \n&\n\nMihta\n \nwal lakula munaia\n)\n\nParam sakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto find out and\n \nmake clear/plain/open, to extract and make clear/plain/open\n \n/\n \ndescubrir y\n\ndejar\n \nclaro/hacer evidente/hacer disponible, extraer y dejar claro/hacer evidente/hacer disponible\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb38\n):\n \nSamson\n \ndîa muni\n \nkarnakira ba, param saki wan wima kaka, lalah ailal maikamna.\n \n–\n \nIf you find out and make\n\nclear to us why Samson is strong, we\n \nwill give you a lot of money.\n \n/ Si se entera y nos deja claro por qué Sa\nn\ns\nó\nn es fuerte,\n\nle daremos mucho dinero.\n)\n\nPliki sakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto search to find\n \n/ buscar para encontrar\n\nPri sakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto free\n \n/ liberar\n\nPri sakaia ba\n \n(\nfg\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nransom\n \n/ rescate\n\nPri sakaia mana\n \n(\ndb,wqu\n-01/24\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nransom, ransom price\n \n/ rescate, precio por el rescate\n\n(Note/Nota: Also:\n \nAtki sakan lâka\n;\n \nkm-2012-15\n \ntranslate\n \nransom\n \nas\n \nAtki sakaia lâka\n;\n \nfg\n \ntranslates\n \nransom\n \nas\n \nPri\nsakaia ba\n;\n \nbh\n \ntranslates as\n \nPri sakaia pura mana ba;\n \ndb-Matiu 20:28\n \ntranslates as\n \nPri sakaia mana\n;\n \ndbta-Matiu\n20:28\n \ntranslates as\n \nSwaki sakanka mana\n \n/ También:\n \nAtki sakan lâka\n;\n \nkm-2012-15\n \ntraduce\n \nrescate\n \ncomo\n \nAtki\nsakaia lâka\n;\n \nfg\n \ntraduce\n \nrescate\n \ncomo\n \nPri sakaia ba\n;\n \nbh\n \nse traduce como\n \nPri sakaia pura mana ba\n;\n \ndb-Matiu 20:28\n\nse traduce como\n \nPri sakaia mana\n;\n \ndbta-Matiu 20:28\n \nse traduce como\n \nSwaki sakanka mana\n)\n\nPri Sasakra\n \n(\ndb\n) (n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nSavior\n \n/ Salvador\n\nSaki\n \n–\n \ntaking out, opening, extracting,\n \nproducing, bearing, finding\n \n/ saca\nndo\n, abri\nendo\n, extra\ny\ne\nndo\n,\n \narrancando,\n\nllev\ná\nndose,\n \nproduci\nendo\n, soport\nando\n,\n \naguantando,\n \nencontra\nndo, consiguiendo, deduciendo, quitando\n\nSaki aik\n \n(\nmy58\n) (v-imp)\n \n–\n \ntake out and bring to me, pick out and bring to me\n \n/ saca y tráeme, escoge y tráeme\n\nSaki briaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto take out to have, to pick out to have, to choose\n \n/ sacar para tener, elegir para tener,\nelegir\n\nSut ba lukanka kumi saki briaia\n \n(\nmwb\n-\n12/18\n)\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto decide unanimously, to choose unanimously\n\n/ decidir por unanimidad, elegir por unanimidad\n\nSaki lulkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto take out and throw away, to remove and reject\n \n/ sacar y tirar, quitar y rechazar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-07/19\n):\n \nRug lâka lukanka taski kum sinski ra balisa kaka, isti saki lulkisna ki?\n \n–\n \nIf an immoral thought\nenters my thinking, do I quickly throw it away?\n \n/ Si un pensamiento inmoral entra en mi mente, ¿lo descarto\nrápidamente?)\n\nSasakra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \none who takes out, one who opens, one who extracts, one who pulls out, one who\ntakes away, one who produces, one who bears, one who finds, one who gets, one who draws\n \n/ uno que saca,\nuno que abre, uno que extrae, uno que produce, uno que lleva, uno que encuentra, uno que consigue, uno que\nhala\n\nLal\n \nmana sasakra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \ntax\n \ncollector\n \n/ recaudador de impuestos\n\nSwaki sasakra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \nsavior, liberator, deliverer\n, rescuer\n \n/ salvador, libertador\n, rescatador\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb77\n):\n \nNaha w\na\nitnika ra walan ningkara, pain wan dara walisa witin sika tasba swaki\n \nsasakrika aihwa ba\n \n–\n\nAfter (we) listened to this man, we really feel that he truly is the real savior\n \n/ Después de que (nosotros)\n\nescuchamos a este hombre, realmente sentimos que él\n \ncierta\nmente es el verdadero salvador\n)\n\nSwaki sasakra daknika\n \n–\n \nrescue team\n \n/ equipo de rescate\n\nSikbi sakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto wash away, to rinse away, to rinse off\n \n/ lavar, enjuagar\n\nSwaki sakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto save\n \n/ salvar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmy49\n):\n \nSwaki wan saks!\n \n–\n \nSave us!\n \n/ ¡Sálvanos!)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb84\n):\n \nDawan swaki ai saks!\n \n–\n \nLord save me!\n \n/ ¡Señor, sálvame!)\n\nSwaki sakan lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsalvation\n \n/ salvación\n\nSwaki sakanka mana\n \n(\ndbta-Matiu 20:28)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nransom\n \n/ rescate\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nPri sakaia\nmana\n)\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \nkm-2012-15\n \ntranslate\n \nransom\n \nas\n \nAtki sakaia lâka\n;\n \nfg\n \ntranslates as\n \nPri sakaia ba;\n \nbh\n \ntranslates as\n \nPri\nsakaia pura mana ba;\n \ndb-Matiu 20:28\n \ntranslates as\n \nPri sakaia mana\n \n/\n \nkm-2012-15\n \ntraduce\n \nrescate\n \ncomo\n \nAtki\nsakaia lâka\n;\n \nfg\n \nse traduce como\n \nPri sakaia ba\n;\n \nbh\n \nse traduce como\n \nPri sakaia pura mana ba\n;\n \ndb-Matiu 20:28\n \nse\ntraduce como\n \nPri sakaia mana\n)\n\nSwaki sasakra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nsavior, liberator, deliverer\n \n/ salvador, libertador\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb77\n):\n \nNaha waitnika ra walan ningkara, pain wan dara walisa witin sika tasba swaki sasakrika aihwa ba\n \n–\n\nAfter (we) listened to this man, we really feel that he truly is the real savior\n \n/ Después de que (nosotros)\nescuchamos a este hombre, realmente sentimos que él realmente es el verdadero salvador)\n\nTaim sakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto take time, to take time out\n \n/ tomarse tiempo",
